WEBVTT

NOTE V2500 HPT Disk Stage 1 — Immersion Scan Tutorial
NOTE Language: English (en)
NOTE Source: Rachel narration via ElevenLabs eleven_multilingual_v2

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.500
V2500 HPT Disk · Stage 1.

2
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:07.000
Immersion scan plan — a full walkthrough.

3
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:10.500
Step 1. Setup the immersion tank.

4
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:13.500
Mount the disk on the turntable, fill the tank,

5
00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.500
and position the probe at an 8-inch water path.

6
00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:19.500
Step 2. Open the scan plan.

7
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:22.500
Select the V2500 Stage 1 preset —

8
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.000
five zones populate automatically from procedure NDIP 1226.

9
00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:29.000
Step 3. Anatomy of the disk.

10
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.000
Five inspection zones —

11
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.000
E, the upper web transition.

12
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.500
A, the upper chamfer.

13
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.000
B, the upper land.

14
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.500
C, the bore entry.

15
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:38.300
D, the bore inner diameter.

16
00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:41.500
Step 4. Zone E plus 45-degree pass.

17
00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:45.500
The probe approaches at plus 45 degrees,
the disk rotates 360,

18
00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:49.500
and the probe steps radially in two-hundredths-inch increments.

19
00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:53.000
Every position is logged into the C-scan.

20
00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:56.500
Step 5. Zone E minus 45-degree pass.

21
00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:00.500
The mirror flips, and we repeat the sweep in the opposite direction

22
00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:02.700
for full bidirectional coverage.

23
00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:06.500
Step 6. Zones A through D.

24
00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:10.500
Each zone is scanned twice, plus and minus 45 degrees —

25
00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:14.500
ten passes in total.

26
00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:17.500
Step 7. Live C-scan capture.

27
00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:21.500
The colormap builds up as the probe moves —

28
00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:25.500
peak amplitude per position, indications above 20% FSH are flagged.

29
00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:27.700
Watch the data come in.

30
00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:31.000
Inspection results.

31
00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:35.000
Five C-scan strips, one per zone —

32
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:38.300
no reportable indications, this disk is clean.

33
00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:41.500
Step 8. Save the scan data.

34
00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:45.400
Enter the part serial number and click Save.

35
00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:48.000
Inspection complete.

36
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Five zones, ten passes, zero indications.
